[ti:(untitled)]
[ar:VESAHE · hkfaduio]
[al:Cinematic & Other]
[by:Radio Vaigyaaniq — draft timing, unverified]
[00:08.00]मच्छर-पंडित संवाद
[00:11.59]Machchar-Pandit Sammwad
[00:15.18]A Conversation Between a Mosquito and a Scholar
[00:18.78]प्रस्तावना Prastāvanā (Introduction)
[00:22.37]A pandit, steeped in the Vedas, sits by the river at dusk, reciting the great mahāvākyas:
[00:25.96]aham brahmasmi … aham dwaitam … aham advaitam … vayam sādhanā asti …
[00:29.55]A mosquito lands on his forearm.
[00:33.14]What follows is not a debate. It is a sammwad—a living dialogue between philosophy and life, between the seeker of stillness and the necessity of hunger, between aham (I) and vayam (we).
[00:36.74]भाग १: प्रथम भेंट Bhāg 1: Pratham Bheṇṭ (First Meeting)
[00:40.33]Machchar (buzzing softly):
[00:43.92]अहम् … अहम् …
[00:47.51]Aham … aham …
[00:51.10]You keep saying I, I.
[00:54.70]But this I — does it itch?
[00:58.29]Pandit (startled):
[01:01.88]You are but a mosquito. I am a knower of Brahman.
[01:05.47]I speak of the Self — the ātman — not this itching skin.
[01:09.06]Machchar:
[01:12.66]Then why did you flinch?
[01:16.25]When I touched you, some I moved.
[01:19.84]Was that Brahman flinching?
[01:23.43]Or was it just you — the one who doesn't want to be touched by me?
[01:27.02]Pandit (irritated):
[01:30.62]You disturb my meditation.
[01:34.21]I am contemplating non-duality — advaita.
[01:37.80]There is no separate you, no separate me.
[01:41.39]We are one.
[01:44.98]Machchar:
[01:48.58]If we are one,
[01:52.17]then when I drink a drop of your blood,
[01:55.76]am I not simply offering ahuti (oblation) to the Self?
[01:59.35]Why do you call it disturbance?
[02:02.94]Why do you raise your hand to strike me?
[02:06.54]Pandit (hand frozen mid-air):
[02:10.13]…
[02:13.72]Machchar:
[02:17.31]You chant vayam sādhanā asti —
[02:20.90]We are the practice.
[02:24.50]But your practice excludes me.
[02:28.09]Your we is only other pandits, other men, other ahams like yours.
[02:31.68]Pandit (slowly lowering hand):
[02:35.27]What do you want, mosquito?
[02:38.86]Machchar:
[02:42.46]Nothing.
[02:46.05]I am already what you are seeking.
[02:49.64]I am the itch in your meditation.
[02:53.23]I am the fragment that breaks your aham brahmasmi into
[02:56.82]aham … aham … aham …
[03:00.42]until you hear not your own voice,
[03:04.01]but the buzzing of the One who speaks through all mouths —
[03:07.60]even this tiny one.
[03:11.19]Pandit (after a long silence):
[03:14.78]Then teach me.
[03:18.38]Machchar:
[03:21.97]I already have.
[03:25.56]You were reciting aham dwaitam, aham advaitam.
[03:29.15]I came as dwaita — the other, the irritant, the small.
[03:32.74]But if you do not kill me,
[03:36.34]you may find I am also advaita —
[03:39.93]the one who makes your aham real
[03:43.52]by being the not-aham that you nevertheless cannot separate from.
[03:47.11]Pandit:
[03:50.70]What is the mantra, then?
[03:54.30]Machchar:
[03:57.89]No mantra.
[04:01.48]Just sit here.
[04:05.07]Let me land.
[04:08.66]Do not flinch.
[04:12.26]Do not kill.
[04:15.85]Let the I that itches and the I that recites
[04:19.44]become one buzz.
[04:23.03]That is vayam.
[04:26.62]Pandit closes his eyes. The mosquito lands again. He does not move.
[04:30.22]Machchar (whispering, or perhaps it is the wind):
[04:33.81]vayam sādhanā asti …
[04:37.40]We are the practice.
[04:40.99]Even this.
[04:44.58]Especially this.
[04:48.18]भाग २: पंडित का विलाप Bhāg 2: Paṇḍit kā Vilāp (The Scholar's Lament)
[04:51.77]दीमी दीमी हम्मmmmmm
[04:55.36]हाय रे मच्छरी तेरी याद आवे है
[04:58.95]Dhīmī dhīmī hmmmmm
[05:02.54]haye re machchharī terī yād āve hai
[05:06.14]Softly, softly… hmmmmm
[05:09.73]Oh, mosquito, your memory comes to me
[05:13.32]Where are you now,
[05:16.91]you who landed on my forearm
[05:20.50]and turned my aham brahmasmi
[05:24.10]into a question mark?
[05:27.69]Your buzz was my first mantra.
[05:31.28]Your itch was my first sparsha (touch)
[05:34.87]that was not mine to control.
[05:38.46]उ पंडित अपने भला कहा
[05:42.06]दुनिया ने झूठ बहकावे है
[05:45.65]U paṇḍit apne bhalā kahā
[05:49.24]duniyā ne jhūṭh bahakāve hai
[05:52.83]That pandit—where is his goodness now?
[05:56.42]The world has deceived him with false lures
[06:00.02]I sat on my āsana,
[06:03.61]wrapped in my shawl of jñāna,
[06:07.20]and called it wisdom.
[06:10.79]But the world—
[06:14.38]the world with its mango blossoms,
[06:17.98]its river at dusk,
[06:21.57]its tiny mosquito—
[06:25.16]whispered a different truth:
[06:28.75]Wisdom that cannot welcome a mosquito
[06:32.34]is not wisdom.
[06:35.94]It is just another fortress.
[06:39.53]You came to me as dwaita—
[06:43.12]the other, the small, the nuisance.
[06:46.71]I wanted advaita—
[06:50.30]the grand, the silent, the undisturbed.
[06:53.90]But you said:
[06:57.49]Let me land. Do not kill. Let the I that itches
[07:01.08]and the I that recites become one buzz.
[07:04.67]And in that moment,
[07:08.26]advaita was not a philosophy.
[07:11.86]It was a mosquito on my skin,
[07:15.45]and my hand not moving.
[07:19.04]Now I sit by the same river.
[07:22.63]I chant vayam sādhanā asti.
[07:26.22]But the we feels incomplete without you.
[07:29.82]दीमी दीमी हम्मmmmmm
[07:33.41]हाय रे मच्छरी तेरी याद आवे है
[07:37.00]Come back, little one.
[07:40.59]Land on me again.
[07:44.18]Let me remember
[07:47.78]that the anthem is not in my chanting alone—
[07:51.37]it is in the buzz I once called disturbance.
